.TH "RECORD\-RUN\.SH" "" "June 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBrecord\-run\.sh\fR
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBrecord\-run\.sh\fR \fIcommand\fR [\fIarg\fR\|\.\|\.\|\.]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBrecord\-run\.sh\fR is a wrapper that executes a command through the RECORD workflow environment\. It sources \fBlib/record\.sh\fR and delegates execution to the \fBrecord_run\fR function defined there, passing all arguments through unchanged\.
.P
This wrapper is typically used to launch commands that should be tracked as part of a RECORD experiment workflow\. It may be invoked directly or submitted as the executable in a Slurm batch job or other batch system, ensuring that commands run within the provenance\-recording environment regardless of execution context\.
.P
If \fBDEBUG\fR is set, entry and exit messages including the full argument list are written to standard error\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
This script accepts no options of its own\. All positional arguments are passed directly to \fBrecord_run\fR\. Refer to the documentation of \fBlib/record\.sh\fR for the arguments and behaviour of \fBrecord_run\fR\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns the exit status of \fBrecord_run\fR\. Returns non\-zero if \fBlib/record\.sh\fR cannot be sourced\.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBDEBUG\fR
When set (to any value), enables entry and exit messages on standard error showing the script name and arguments\.
.P
All environment variables required by \fBlib/record\.sh\fR and \fBrecord_run\fR are inherited from the calling environment\. Refer to \fBlib/record\.sh\fR for the full list\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Run a command under RECORD provenance tracking:
.IP "" 4
.nf
record\-run\.sh my_sim \-\-config=conf\.yaml input\.dat
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Submit as a Slurm batch job:
.IP "" 4
.nf
sbatch \-\-wrap="record\-run\.sh my_sim \-\-config=conf\.yaml input\.dat"
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
Use from a Slurm job script:
.IP "" 4
.nf
#!/usr/bin/env bash
#SBATCH \-\-job\-name=my_sim
record\-run\.sh my_sim \-\-config=conf\.yaml input\.dat
.fi
.IP "" 0
