.SH "BUGS"
The \fBDEBUG\fR check \fB[ \-n $DEBUG ]\fR is unquoted; when \fBDEBUG\fR is unset the expression becomes \fB[ \-n ]\fR, which evaluates to true in bash (since the single token \fB\-n\fR is treated as a non\-empty string)\. As a result the entry and exit messages are always printed to standard error regardless of whether \fBDEBUG\fR is set\. The correct form is \fB[ \-n "$DEBUG" ]\fR\.
.P
\fBlib/record\.sh\fR is sourced with a path relative to the working directory rather than relative to the script's own location\. If \fBrecord\-run\.sh\fR is invoked from a directory other than the RECORD project root, sourcing will fail\.
.P
The script sources \fBlib/record\.sh\fR rather than \fBlib\.record\.common\.sh\fR used by the other RECORD wrapper scripts, which is an inconsistency in the library path convention across the suite\.
